<article class="env-lemma" id="05LU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05LU">Lemma <span data-tag="05LU">15.19.5</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/05LP" data-tag="05LP">15.19.1</a>. Let $I \subset R$ be an ideal. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R$ is a Noetherian ring, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S$ is a Noetherian ring, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$M$ is a finite $S$-module, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for each $n \geq 1$ and any prime $\mathfrak q \in V(J + IS)$ the module $(M/I^ n M)_{\mathfrak q}$ is flat over $R/I^ n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then (<a href="/tag/05LQ" data-tag="05LQ">15.19.1.1</a>) holds for $(R, I)$, i.e., for every prime $\mathfrak q \in V(J + IS)$ the localization $M_{\mathfrak q}$ is flat over $R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak q \in V(J + IS)$. Then Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0523" data-tag="0523">10.99.11</a> applied to $R \to S_{\mathfrak q}$ and $M_{\mathfrak q}$ implies that $M_{\mathfrak q}$ is flat over $R$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>